## Session 16 — summary (criteria NOT met, marker not written)

**The 8/tcp blocker is `dir_reuse_coherency`** — a durable cross-node dir-block lost-update (a peer writes a block with 126 entries, another node clobbers it back to 77). This session **decisively narrowed** it and built most of a fix.

**Major decisive results (all instrumented, RULE 4):**
1. **Double-grant RULED OUT** — built an always-on `MX-DOUBLEGRANT` master-table auditor (KEEP); fired **zero** times on a failing run, disproving the TCP-double-grant root assumed since sess49. The DLM serializes EX correctly.
2. **No mht value reliably passes** — it fails at mht=300 too (the "mht tradeoff" and "16/17 baseline" were lucky runs of a **timing race**, which dirwr/instr tracing masks). The bug must be eliminated, not tuned around.
3. **Acquire-side disk-compare refresh is structurally racy**; coherence must be tied to grant tenure.
4. Refuted ~8 fix levers (force_coherent, postread_reread, release_invalidate, release_fua, leaf-refresh [caught+reverted a regression], prior-tenure evict, pre-read epoch check).
5. **Root of why the tenure-epoch approach didn't converge:** `i_dlm_dir_valid_epoch` **lags real handoffs** (set only at reload-end, after keep-guards that short-circuit) — measured valid_epoch=66 vs master grant_epoch=70. The comparison must use the **master's authoritative `mxfs_v5_dlm_inode_dir_epoch`**.

**In-progress fix (build E3CDB9F1, compiles, all gated OFF = safe baseline == 48C6A95E):** full tenure-epoch plumbing (`b_mxfs_dir_epoch` field, stamps at dir-block create/modify, pre-read + evict-override checks). The pre-read **check** was just switched to the master epoch; the **stamps** still need the same swap (precise sites listed in memory). Next session: finish the stamp swap, enable `dir_evict_prior_tenure=1`, validate at dirwr=0 across ≥5 runs; fall back to GPT's release-side REVOKING fence if it still fails.

